A||||32||Cliff Pennock||Just thinking out loud...||||1||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||12-14-2001||08:12 AM||||So this is what the world has come to. 3 Million years of evolution and instead of using stones and wooden spears, we use computers and airplanes. We are no better than we were then. In fact, we are worse than we were then. We have found faster and more efficient ways to kill the inhabitants of this planet. We no longer kill because we have to, but because we can. And preferably by the thousands. We do not tolerate the masses and we do not tolerate the individual. We still have to piss in every corner of our territory. Or better yet, boobytrap it so the intruder will not make the same mistake twice.<P>It's strange because everywhere you look, people are preaching that we have come a long way. That we are not the barbarians we once were. That we are now free to speak our minds. That we are more tolerant. But the only reason we have become more tolerant is because we have almost eliminated all that we found intolerant.<P>We're a a strange species. By some stroke of incredible luck we were given a home to live in. One that should last forever. A home that would feed us and give us shelter. A home that was much larger than what we actually needed. And all we had to do was live in peace with those we had to share it with. But instead we put all our might, all our intelligence and all our energy in finding ways to destroy it as quickly as possible. And that's our biggest feat to date. We have made species extinct. We have depleted our home from its natural resources. We have managed to cause irreversibly damage. We're a strange species indeed.<P>And in our greatest hour, with almost nothing left to destroy, and bored of killing flies with a spray can, we seek for new challenges. And we have found the greatest challenge of all. We have found a new enemy so ferocious, so dangerous and so intelligent we can't stand it. There's no room for the both of us. And as we look in the mirror we are pondering on ways to kill this new enemy.<P>Yes, we have come a long way. We've reached the point of subconscious realization that we need to focus our energy on destroying this planet's largest pest: ourselves. Because we have proven that we are not worthy of being earth's dominant species. Because we are filled with hate. Because we will never learn to love each other.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||12-14-2001||08:30 AM||||It's not a popular viewpoint.. but I agree.<P>Every organism reaches an equilibrium with it's environment.. except humans. We breed, use up all the resources.. then move on, leaving pollution and waste behind.. The only other organism that does this, is cancer.. (yes I know this is from a movie...)<P>We've done more harm to this planet in the last 60 years than in the entire 4.5 billion years the earth has been here..<P>(bosses just walked back in. gotta get back to work, will post more later)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Patrick's Dad||12-14-2001||09:18 AM||||This surprises you? We've had plenty of warning....<P>"...For men will becoame lovers of themselves, lovers of money, boasters, proud, blasphemers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy, unloving, unforgiving, slanderers, without self-control, brutal, despisers of good, traitors, headstrong, haughty, lovers of pleasure rather tna lovers of God, having a form of godliness but denying its power." 2 Timothy 3:2-5a<P>The forum itself is a microcosm of the world in which we live. We are so wrapped up in our own views and "freedom of speech" that we forget (or ignore) the rights and sensibilities not only of other rightful members, but its owner.<P>I'm not suggesting, Cliff, that you destroy the forum in a flood, but, if so bent, you understand better what a sovereign Creator must feel looking down on our race. In either case, we have but ourselves to blame. Ultimately, this is a function of Lowest Common Denominator Marketing (Not capitalism, mind you). The needs of the many may out outweigh the needs of the few or the one, but true prosperity comes from the needs of the few and the one attended to. OTOH, the rants of the one (be they OBL or EdB52) can make things, well, unfun.<P>We will, unfortunately, go through much more of this than this, in both forums  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> . Makes you want to have kids, huh? (I have two.)||||reg||2
Z||000003||deceler8||12-14-2001||09:19 AM||||While a lot of individuals have evolved beyond the cycle of violence, clearly the species has not.<P>But the fact that individuals have evolved means all is not lost for the species. And, unfortunately, perhaps the only way the species as a whole gets to that point is to let natural selection take its course. Translation...kill the bad guys.<P>Not a pretty scenario, huh ?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sage||12-14-2001||09:29 AM||||Cliff:<P>That could have been one of mine, a few years ago.<P>Just remember, we are ALL on the path, just some know it some don't.<P>To one who knows, no explanation is necessary, to one who doesn't, none is possible.<P><BR>  Yes, absolutely, we are our own worst enemy.<BR>Robert Frost said; "In three words I can sum up everything I've learned about life;  It goes on."  <P>Be patient, yea I know how hard that can be, people dying and killing each other, the prejudice, intolerance, bigotry, self centeredness that plagues us all sometimes gets to be too much, but you can't "rip the skin from the snake" it must molt at it's own rate.  Be patient with he who is dying as well as he who is being born.  Meaning generations as well as the inner self that is constantly reinventing itself, at least in a naturally developing human being.<P>No matter what your stance, there will always be someone opposing it, after all, black is not black without white, and like I used to tell my boys, "If you don't like the way somebody else is, don't be that way yourself!" <P>Ok, I'm done for now, just rambling out loud in your out loud thought.<P>Patience is the greatest virtue, for with it, all else is attainable.<P>Peace<P> <P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000005||frontal lobe||12-14-2001||10:37 AM||||You figured it out, Cliff.<P>People are still people, just with different background now than years ago.<P>It is interesting, though...except that it is often too sad how people treat each other to just be passively interested.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Little Duce Coupe||12-14-2001||11:05 AM||||<BR>Ditto ~ not popular but true.<P>Humans have one ability that animals never developed that is the support of this fact.  Is it tools, humor, war,love, hate, etc..etc.....no... oh no these are too easy, I would argue that one ability is DENIAL that ability to act one way but argue the opposite.<P>To over simplfy: <P>Humans are they yeast to this planets bottle of wine....and through denial some day this speciase will choke on its own discharges, after it has used all the good within the bottle.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||12-14-2001||11:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>We're a a strange species. By some stroke of incredible luck we were given a home to live in. One that should last forever. A home that would feed us and give us shelter. A home that was much larger than what we actually needed. And all we had to do was live in peace with those we had to share it with. But instead we put all our might, all our intelligence and all our energy in finding ways to destroy it as quickly as possible. And that's our biggest feat to date. We have made species extinct. We have depleted our home from its natural resources. We have managed to cause irreversibly damage. We're a strange species indeed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In the grand scheme of things, I don't think that anything that humankind has done is either permanent or irreversible. <P>If we offend Mother Nature too much, she'll just do a "housecleaning".<P>She could make life very difficult, if not impossible, for us. <P>Then, in a few hundred or a few thousand years or whatever, she'd start over.    <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
