Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||12-14-2001||01:37 PM||||there most certainly IS an answer:<P> "Whoever would follow me must hate his mother and father, and hate his own life!" -JC<P> "do not walk in the flesh anylonger, but walk in the Spirit"<P> Suicide is almost the correct answer - when you come to the point in you life where you realize there is no hope for humanity, and no hope for yourself, that is when you are ready to let go of your life as you have known it<P> and let God show you the right way - then the life you lived before ends, and you are like a new creation.<P> I firmly believe its the only hope for us as individuals, and for humanity as a whole. Nobody is going to stand up one sunny day and say "HEY LETS ALL BE NICE AND STOP KILLING EACH OTHER" and change the world.<P> Its only when God Himself interviens in our lives, as individuals, one by one, that we change, and the world changes.<P> An honest assesment of the fallen state of humanity is the first step.<P> Asking God to take over control of your life personally is the next.||||reg||1
