Z||000021||AkursedX||12-14-2001||10:56 PM||||Well Ken, I would have to agree with your idea.  (Although the whole Jesus thing simply doesn not appeal to me.  I'm not a fan of organized religion.  But nor do I denouce it.  It is good for some people, and for others it isn't.  It's as simple as that.)<P>But your basic idea is true.  If you spend your time dwelling on your hatred of humanity and of yourself, you will reach a point where you will (A.) Kill yourself, or (B.)  find something to live for.  That something can be a variety of things, whether it be finding religion, or having some sort of personal goal to do what you can to make this world a better place.  But it is something that is eventually accepted.<P>But we humans are a strange creature.  It is because of the extremes we can achieve.  We can love something so much that we are willing to give anything, even our lives for it, and yet we can also hate something so much that we are willing to give anything, even our lives to see it destroyed.....<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||ray b||12-14-2001||11:34 PM||||cliff you have made the world a better place by this forum people have become friends by meeting here.with out you they may never have known each other at all. as all friendship is very good karma you have created<BR>good, what better can I say of a man.<BR>there is no magic bullit or quick fix but if each tryes a little in their own way to make things a little better slowly things change.<BR>we do progress slowly and slip back but BIG EVIL like the NAZI, or empires or slaves or world wars of our past are not now or real threats to come again.so remember it could be better but it HAS BEEN A LOT WORSE and it ain't finished just yet.<BR>THE first part of any fix is to know you have a problem then deside how to fix and we are just waking up to realize there is A PROBLEM now.<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||fogglethorpe||12-15-2001||02:39 PM||||War has existed since mankind has existed, and always will. We will never be able to eliminate it, and it is naive to think we ever will. Even if some entity such as the United Nations attempted to band together and "impose peace",it will not be peace if it's forced.<BR>That being said, I believe there is righteous war, and evil war. The war America is currently engaged in is righteous. We are not an imperialist state...we are lovers of freedom and peace, and try to promote that around the world, as we should. Those who hate us really hate peace, and freedom, and we are fighting to preserve it.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Mach10||12-15-2001||03:07 PM||||The "Survival of the Fittest" no longer applies to humans, as a group. Some 40-thousand years ago, humans pretty much STOPPED physically evolving. This was due to a VERY important change. We woke up. Our brains started working. Instead of the efficient, but slow method of survival, i.e., darwinism, we started a new trend, called "Cultural Evolution." If it got cold out, we didn't grow fur, we kill minks and make coats. We can't over-power a bear, so we invent remmingtons. We are by definition an enlightened society. We can survive in ANY climate, because we can make the necessary changes CONSCIOUSLY, instead of having to wait 3000 generations for the right random mutation to show up.<P>On the other hand, old habits die hard. We still fight and battle for territory, be it intellectual, or geographical. We still fight over mates. We still break out the colored plumage to court.<P>So we have this inherent identity crisis. We act like animals, but we're supposed to have transcended beyond. As a species, we are more or less following the same pattern as a locust swarm. Sad part is, locusts invariable run out of food, and all but a few die out. That's what our fate is. but if we're lucky, it won't happen in OUR lifetime... But this attitude is what our problem is. Nobody CARES what's going to happen in 500 years, so we carry on.<P><BR>||||reg||12
Z||000025||GTFiero1||12-15-2001||06:50 PM||||everybody has a different vision for the perfect world. thus that is why we have corruption today. Bin Ladin killed those people in the planes and the towers because he thought that we are all bad and he would bring soem peace to the world, but we think that he is bad because he killed innocent people but he belived he killed awful sinners. Animals dont have to worry about the perfect world because they lack many of the skills we have. i dont think this is coming out the way i want it cause its hard to put it into words. <P>If everybody was equal and we were all civilized then life would be completely different. You, me may never have existed because of the great events that changed people and there way of life. with out WW1 then maybe two people never would have met and never gotten married and had kids who grew up and became senators, governers, military leaders or you or I. i know if WW2 never happened then one of my friend would never had existed or i would never exist. If we didnt "rob the planet of its resources" than there may not be power plants, hospitals, or cars and a beloved fiero would have never existed but that wouldnt matter to us than because we would have no idea the car or the fiero was. <P>Its in our nature to destroy ourselves to meet what we think is right. We have become better than what we use to be though. Romans, when there child was first born, use to leave there baby out side over night and if it got sick, they would leave it to die, if it didnt get sick they would keep and raise it. We dont do this anymore. <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000026||Mach10||12-15-2001||06:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>everybody has a different vision for the perfect world. thus that is why we have corruption today. Bin Ladin killed those people in the planes and the towers because he thought that we are all bad and he would bring soem peace to the world, but we think that he is bad because he killed innocent people but he belived he killed awful sinners. Animals dont have to worry about the perfect world because they lack many of the skills we have. i dont think this is coming out the way i want it cause its hard to put it into words. <P>If everybody was equal and we were all civilized then life would be completely different. You, me may never have existed because of the great events that changed people and there way of life. with out WW1 then maybe two people never would have met and never gotten married and had kids who grew up and became senators, governers, military leaders or you or I. i know if WW2 never happened then one of my friend would never had existed or i would never exist. If we didnt "rob the planet of its resources" than there may not be power plants, hospitals, or cars and a beloved fiero would have never existed but that wouldnt matter to us than because we would have no idea the car or the fiero was. <P>Its in our nature to destroy ourselves to meet what we think is right. We have become better than what we use to be though. Romans, when there child was first born, use to leave there baby out side over night and if it got sick, they would leave it to die, if it didnt get sick they would keep and raise it. We dont do this anymore. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>For a 16-year old, you sure have a pretty good grasp of human nature... A young anthropologist to be?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>You think the romans are bad? Try some of the MODERN people. In small Hunter-gatherer societies, population MUST be controlled. They do this by practicing Female Infanticide. If it doesn't have a penis and/or they already HAVE a daughter... I'll spare you the details. <P>Amazingly enough, this is from the more peaceful and gentle societies. NEVER underestimate the destructive ability of <I>Homo Sapiens Sapiens</I>||||reg||14
