Z||000032||Adeptus||12-17-2001||03:06 PM||||I'm pretty new to the board here, but I think I should put in my 2 cents in this one.<BR>     There is a ton of BS going on in the world lately, but then again this has always been going on since the first time some caveman picked up a rock, and bashed the head of another caveman to get the better and warmer cave in which to live. I believe that we are still evolving, but it's more of a intellectual evolution. The more we know, the more we understand. The more we understand, the more we grow, not just as individuals, but as a species as a whole. The real threat comes when we decide NOT to learn and understand, that promotes ignorance, and the consequences of which are intolerance, arrogance, and other negative mindsets. Eventually I think we will outgrow our more destructive impulses, but it will take each person to do help achieve this. Only through acquiring knowledge and striving to be the best human beings we can will we help those around us to do the same.<BR>Humanity will always define itself by it's struggles, and through those struggles we become stronger. This episode in history will pass and we will be stronger in the end for it. ||||reg||1
